---
// src/pages/about/_components/AboutHero.astro
import Section from '../../../components/ui/Section.astro';
---

<Section class="relative pt-8 sm:pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-10 md:pb-16 lg:pb-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <div
    class="absolute top-[-10%] right-[-5%] w-[600px] h-[600px] bg-amber-500/10 rounded-full blur-[100px] pointer-events-none"
  >
  </div>
  <div
    class="absolute bottom-[10%] left-[-10%] w-[500px] h-[500px] bg-emerald-700/10 rounded-full blur-[100px] pointer-events-none"
  >
  </div>

  <div
    class="max-w-7xl mx-auto grid lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center relative z-10"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <div
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest rounded-full mb-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        Our Story
      </div>

      <h1
        class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl lg:leading-[1.1] font-bold text-emerald-950 tracking-tight mb-8"
      >
        A community of masters, <br />
        <em class="font-serif italic text-emerald-700 font-medium">not just teachers.</em>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-lg text-emerald-900/80 font-medium leading-relaxed mb-10 max-w-xl">
        Here, every instructor is an academy unto themselves. We built Quranific to bridge a massive
        gap in online Islamic education: tech platforms that didn't understand the tradition, and
        traditional academies that lacked reliable technology. We brought them together.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="max-w-xs">
          <div class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-1 leading-tight">
            Trusted by families
          </div>
          <div
            class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-900/60 uppercase tracking-wide leading-relaxed"
          >
            across the UK, US, UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Canada, Australia, Europe, and Singapore.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-1">2021</div>
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-900/60 uppercase tracking-wide">
            Year Founded
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-emerald-950 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-10 relative overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
      <div
        class="absolute bottom-[-10%] right-[-10%] w-[200px] h-[200px] bg-white/5 rounded-full blur-xl pointer-events-none"
      >
      </div>
      <div
        class="absolute top-[-5%] left-[-5%] w-[120px] h-[120px] bg-amber-500/10 rounded-full blur-xl pointer-events-none"
      >
      </div>

      <div
        class="font-serif text-[60px] leading-[0.5] text-white/10 mb-2 font-black"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        "
      </div>
      <p
        class="font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl italic text-white/95 leading-relaxed mb-6 relative z-10"
      >
        I spent years formally training as an Islamic scholar, proofreading complex classical texts
        in Hadith, Fiqh, and Tafsir. But as my career in software engineering grew, I noticed a
        massive disconnect in how the Quran was being taught online. Families abroad were looking
        for authentic teachers, but the platforms connecting them were chaotic. Local classes were
        overcrowded, and online options were plagued by dropped calls, rotating tutors, and zero
        accountability. I didn't want to just complain about the standard of online Islamic
        education. I wanted to build the infrastructure to fix it.
      </p>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 relative z-10 pt-5 border-t border-white/10">
        <div
          class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-white/10 border border-white/20 flex items-center justify-center font-serif text-xl text-white font-bold shrink-0"
        >
          ف
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white text-base">Faisal Khan</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-emerald-100/70 font-medium">Founder & CEO, Quranific</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
